14. Common Interview Comparisons
| FileReader | BufferedReader |
| ---------- | -------------- |
| Slow       | Fast           |
| Reads char | Reads line     |
| No buffer  | Uses buffer    |

| IO           | NIO           |
| ------------ | ------------- |
| Blocking     | Non-blocking  |
| Stream-based | Channel-based |
| Slower       | Faster        |

15. Common Tricky Interview Questions (4+ Years)
Q1. Difference between byte & character streams?
Byte → binary
Character → text (Unicode)

Q2. Why BufferedReader is faster?
Reads data in chunks instead of char-by-char

Q3. Why use NIO?
Performance, scalability, cleaner API

Q4. What is transient?
Prevents field serialization

Q5. How to handle large files?
Buffered streams
Files.lines()
Streaming

